#set page(paper: "a4", margin: (x: 22mm, y: 20mm), fill: rgb("#f8f5ee"))
#set text(font: "Libertinus Serif", size: 11pt, fill: rgb("#25352f"))
#set par(leading: 0.7em)
#let accent = rgb("#b85d42")
#let label(body) = text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 8pt, fill: accent, tracking: 0.08em, body)
#grid(columns: (1fr, auto), [#label[FIELD NOTES  /  01]], [#label[A JOURNAL OF ATTENTION]])
#v(13mm)
#text(size: 43pt, weight: "bold")[The art of\ noticing]
#v(5mm)
#text(size: 15pt, style: "italic", fill: rgb("#69776e"))[A quieter way to see the everyday.]
#v(10mm)
#line(length: 100%, stroke: 0.7pt + rgb("#aab8aa"))
#v(9mm)
#grid(columns: (1fr, 1fr), gutter: 10mm,
  [
    #text(size: 25pt, fill: accent)[A] good walk begins without an agenda. The
    familiar street becomes a collection of small discoveries: a shadow moving
    across a wall, a window left open, the first green leaf after a long winter.

    Noticing is not a special talent. It is a practice of making room for what
    is already there.
  ],
  [
    Slow down long enough and the ordinary starts to offer its own kind of
    abundance. A moment of attention can make a familiar place feel entirely new.

    #v(3mm)
    #text(size: 16pt, style: "italic", fill: accent)[“Attention is a form of generosity.”]
    #v(3mm)

    Keep a page for the things that catch your eye. A color, a sentence, the
    shape of a cloud: each note is an invitation to return to the present.
  ],
)
#v(1fr)
#line(length: 100%, stroke: 0.5pt + rgb("#aab8aa"))
#v(3mm)
#grid(columns: (1fr, auto), [#label[THE SLOW EDIT  /  SPRING 2026]], [#label[01]])
